<div
class="panel-card span-4-cols"
style="
background:#060a12;
border:1px solid rgba(6,182,212,0.2);
margin-top:0.25rem;
">

<div>

<h3
class="card-block-title"
style="color:var(--quantum-cyan);">
System Metric Calculations Playbook
</h3>

<p
class="card-block-sub"
style="color:#64748b;">
These formulas are learning models. They are useful for structured self-observation, not clinical or scientific diagnostic measurements.
</p>

</div>


<div class="calc-matrix-grid">


<div class="calc-sheet">

<h4>
⚡ [A] Attention Field
</h4>

<p>
Estimate how much of a work period remained devoted to the intended task.
</p>

<div class="math-image-box">

<div class="formula-box">

AFS =
(Deep Focus Minutes ÷ Available Work Minutes)
× 100

</div>

</div>

<p
style="
font-size:0.7rem;
background:rgba(255,255,255,0.01);
padding:0.3rem;
border-radius:3px;
">

<strong>Example:</strong>

75 minutes of focused work during a 90-minute block:

<br>

<span
style="
color:var(--matrix-green);
font-family:var(--font-mono);
">

(75 ÷ 90) × 100 = 83.3%

</span>

</p>

</div>


<div class="calc-sheet">

<h4>
📈 [B] Behavioral Flow
</h4>

<p>
Measure execution reliability by comparing completed actions with planned actions.
</p>

<div class="math-image-box">

<div class="formula-box">

Behavior Yield =
Completed ÷ Planned × 100

</div>

</div>

<p
style="
font-size:0.7rem;
background:rgba(255,255,255,0.01);
padding:0.3rem;
border-radius:3px;
">

<strong>Example:</strong>

3 completed actions from 5 planned actions:

<br>

<span
style="
color:var(--alert-amber);
font-family:var(--font-mono);
">

(3 ÷ 5) × 100 = 60%

</span>

</p>

</div>


<div class="calc-sheet">

<h4>
⚓ [L] Leverage Index
</h4>

<p>
Estimate whether an activity produces relatively large impact for its required effort.
</p>

<div class="math-image-box">

<div class="formula-box">

L =
Impact Score ÷ Effort Score

</div>

</div>

<p
style="
font-size:0.7rem;
background:rgba(255,255,255,0.01);
padding:0.3rem;
border-radius:3px;
">

<strong>Example:</strong>

An automation has an impact score of 9 and effort score of 3:

<br>

<span
style="
color:var(--matrix-green);
font-family:var(--font-mono);
">

9 ÷ 3 = 3.0x

</span>

</p>

</div>


<div class="calc-sheet">

<h4>
⚙ [E] Environment
</h4>

<p>
Audit whether the environment makes productive behavior easier to initiate.
</p>


<div class="audit-check-row">

<div class="check-node">

<strong>+20%</strong>

Tool Ready

</div>

<div class="check-node">

<strong>+20%</strong>

Phone Hidden

</div>

<div class="check-node">

<strong>+20%</strong>

Task Staged

</div>

<div class="check-node">

<strong>+20%</strong>

Distractions Blocked

</div>

<div class="check-node">

<strong>+20%</strong>

Resources Ready

</div>

</div>


<p
style="
font-size:0.7rem;
margin-top:0.4rem;
color:var(--text-high);
">

The goal is not a perfect score. The goal is to discover which environmental changes make the desired behavior easier.

</p>

</div>


